# Bench.h/Bench.c mirror what tools/typesupport generates for a .msg, deliberately and by hand:
# the same PascalCase type and PascalCase_verb codec functions, the same wire numbers stated as
# literals in _Static_asserts, the same tt_Topic global named after the type. That shape is fixed
# by the codec ABI in tickle.h, not chosen here, so the project's own lower_case convention cannot
# apply without breaking the shared function-pointer typedefs - exactly the reasoning examples/
# uint64/.clang-tidy and tools/typesupport/tests/golden/.clang-tidy already carry for the
# genuinely generated copies. Written by hand rather than generated only because this scenario's
# struct predates wiring the generator into examples/perf_hil (see Bench.h's own header comment).
#
# Added 2026-09-23, when `make lint` was made runnable again: this directory was the one place with
# generator-shaped code and no such file, so it produced every remaining warning in the tree - and
# a lint target that cannot be run clean is one people route around, which is how two red mains
# happened in a day.
#
# InheritParentConfig keeps everything else on (bugprone-*, the rest of readability-*/misc-*/
# performance-*), so a real defect here still fails.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-readability-identifier-naming,-readability-magic-numbers'
